Z||000000||Shiner||02-17-2001||02:01 AM||||"DEARBORN, Mich. (Reuters) - Ford Motor Co. said on Friday it was recalling more than 710,000 of its popular pickup trucks and Mercury brand minivans because of possible problems with their fuel systems that could result in fire.<BR>The world's No. 2 automaker said the recall involved 435,426 Mercury Villager minivans made between November 1991 and June 1998 and 275,000 of its F-Series trucks manufactured from December 1992 until August 1993."<P><P>------------------<BR>-Shiner-<BR>'84 Sport Coupe<BR>'87 GT<BR>'86 SE 2M6 (parts car)||||reg||1
